Subject: dts: be7000: reserve the TrustZone app and boot chain regions like stock

Stock reserves tzapp@49b00000 (6 MB) and rsvd1@4fa00000, rsvd2@4fb00000
(256 KB each) as no-map. Our DTS did not, so /proc/iomem showed them as
System RAM and Linux could hand out pages the secure side may still use.
Reserve them the same way. Costs about 6.5 MB of MemTotal.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
@@ -135,6 +135,24 @@
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		/* Same as stock: TrustZone applications and two regions of the
+		 * boot chain. Without them Linux hands this memory out as normal
+		 * RAM although the secure side may still write to it. */
+		tzapp@49b00000 {
+			no-map;
+			reg = <0x0 0x49b00000 0x0 0x600000>;
+		};
+
+		rsvd1@4fa00000 {
+			no-map;
+			reg = <0x0 0x4fa00000 0x0 0x40000>;
+		};
+
+		rsvd2@4fb00000 {
+			no-map;
+			reg = <0x0 0x4fb00000 0x0 0x40000>;
+		};
+
 		q6_region: wcnss@4ab00000 {
 			no-map;
 			reg = <0x0 0x4ab00000 0x0 0x2b00000>;
